-  // insert a clone of the most recent X-defining instruction (LastX16Writer)
-  // immediately after the REP that re-enters 16-bit X mode, before the READ.
-  //
-  // Background: on the 65816, SEP #$10 physically zeroes the high bytes of
-  // both X and Y. A REP #$10 later makes the full 16-bit register accessible
-  // again but does NOT restore the high byte -- it stays 0. Any instruction
